---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Nav from "../../components/Nav.astro";
const codespaceUrl = "https://codespaces.new/hackus-mans/portofolio?quickstart=1";
---
<BaseLayout title="Linux Lab — GitHub Codespaces" description="Launch a personal Linux lab from the portfolio using GitHub Codespaces.">
  <Nav />
  <main class="sandbox-main">
    <section class="sandbox-hero wrap">
      <div>
        <span class="card-label">GITHUB CODESPACES / PERSONAL LAB</span>
        <h1>Launch a real Linux lab.</h1>
        <p>One click creates a real cloud development environment from this repository. The lab is attached to the visitor's own GitHub account — no shared VPS and no access to the portfolio server.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href={codespaceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Launch Linux Lab ↗</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/hackus-mans/portofolio/tree/main/.devcontainer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect configuration</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sandbox-policy">
        <div><span>PLATFORM</span><strong>GitHub Codespaces</strong></div>
        <div><span>OS</span><strong>Ubuntu 24.04</strong></div>
        <div><span>USER</span><strong>non-root developer</strong></div>
        <div><span>WORKSPACE</span><strong>personal copy</strong></div>
        <div><span>TOOLS</span><strong>Python · GCC · Git · Nmap</strong></div>
        <div><span>PERSISTENCE</span><strong>until user deletes it</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sandbox-workspace wrap">
      <div class="codespace-preview">
        <div class="real-terminal-titlebar">
          <div class="window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
          <span>codespace@linux-lab — ~/lab</span>
          <span>visitor-owned environment</span>
        </div>
        <div class="codespace-terminal">
          <p><span>$</span> whoami</p>
          <strong>vscode</strong>
          <p><span>$</span> pwd</p>
          <strong>/workspaces/portofolio/lab</strong>
          <p><span>$</span> python3 --version</p>
          <strong>Python 3.x</strong>
          <p><span>$</span> nmap --version</p>
          <strong>Nmap available</strong>
          <p><span>$</span> cat README.md</p>
          <strong>Welcome to the Linux practice lab.</strong>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="codespace-flow">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h2>Click launch</h2>
          <p>GitHub opens the Codespaces creation screen for this repository.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h2>GitHub builds it</h2>
          <p>The checked-in devcontainer installs the lab environment automatically.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h2>Use real Linux</h2>
          <p>The visitor gets VS Code in the browser plus an actual terminal and writable workspace.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>04</span>
          <h2>Delete when done</h2>
          <p>Closing the tab does not instantly erase a Codespace. The visitor can stop or delete it from GitHub when finished.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="sandbox-footnote">
        <p><strong>Important:</strong> usage belongs to the GitHub account that creates the Codespace. Visitors must sign in to GitHub.</p>
        <p>This removes the need for DigitalOcean or another VPS for the lab experience.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
